  "description_short": "Riverside hotel restaurant in Klein Brak River offering relaxed meals with convenient pool and bar access.",
  "description_long": "Set along the Klein Brak River off the R102, Brinkleys River Village serves as both accommodation hub and casual dining spot for locals and travellers exploring the Garden Route. The restaurant caters to hotel guests and drop-ins alike, with a menu that covers breakfast through dinner in a laid-back atmosphere.\n\nThe setting takes advantage of its riverside location, with outdoor seating areas and proximity to the hotel's pool facilities. It's a convenient stop between George and Mossel Bay, offering straightforward pub-style fare and basic meals without pretension. The attached bar and liquor store make it a practical choice for groups staying in the area or passing through.\n\nWhile it functions primarily as a hotel restaurant, Brinkleys fills a gap in the Klein Brak River dining scene with its accessible location just off the main road and facilities that accommodate families, sports groups, and event gatherings throughout the year.",
